WEBVTT

00:17.250 --> 00:19.250
[♪ Nat King Cole: "Orange Colored Sky"]

00:24.208 --> 00:26.125
<i>♪ I was walking along ♪</i>

00:26.125 --> 00:28.291
<i>♪ Mindin' my business ♪</i>

00:28.291 --> 00:31.708
<i>♪ When out of an orange-colored sky ♪</i>

00:31.708 --> 00:35.875
<i>♪ Flash, bam, alakazam ♪</i>

00:35.875 --> 00:38.250
<i>♪ Wonderful you came by ♪</i>

00:38.250 --> 00:40.791
<i>♪ I was hummin' a tune ♪</i>

00:40.791 --> 00:43.166
<i>♪ Drinkin' in sunshine ♪</i>

00:43.166 --> 00:46.500
<i>♪ When out of that orange-colored view ♪</i>

00:46.500 --> 00:49.791
<i>♪ Flash, bam, alakazam ♪</i>

00:49.791 --> 00:53.125
<i>♪ I got a look at you ♪</i>

00:53.125 --> 00:56.041
<i>♪ One look and I yelled "timber"...</i>

00:56.041 --> 00:58.750
[newscaster] [over radio] <i>...negotiations
were scheduled to continue today</i>

00:58.750 --> 01:01.916
<i>as the White House had no comment
about the President's whereabouts.</i>

01:01.916 --> 01:03.500
<i>♪ And the bottom fell out,
I went into a spin ♪</i>

01:03.500 --> 01:05.750
<i>♪ And I started to shout,
"I've been hit..."</i>

01:05.750 --> 01:07.833
[Mr. Handy] Ready to be of service, madam.

01:07.833 --> 01:09.833
[news anchor] <i>...between
America and her adversaries</i>

01:09.833 --> 01:12.666
<i>crumbled this morning
in Anchorage, Alaska.</i>

01:12.666 --> 01:15.583
<i>The specter of nuclear war
facing this nation</i>

01:15.583 --> 01:17.583
<i>for ten long years is final...</i>

01:17.583 --> 01:19.083
<i>♪ Alakazam...</i>

01:19.083 --> 01:21.666
It's a party, let's just...
focus on the party.

01:21.666 --> 01:23.708
- Okay?
- <i>♪ Purple-striped ♪</i>

01:23.708 --> 01:27.000
<i>♪ Pretty green polka-dot sky ♪</i>

01:27.000 --> 01:31.333
<i>♪ Flash, bam, alakazam ♪</i>

01:31.333 --> 01:33.750
<i>♪ And goodbye ♪</i>

01:33.750 --> 01:35.708
[cheering]

01:38.416 --> 01:40.000
All right, birthday boy.

01:40.000 --> 01:42.625
Let's get a photo of you
up here on Sugarfoot.

01:42.625 --> 01:46.541
Why the hell is Cooper Howard
working kids' birthday parties?

01:46.541 --> 01:49.041
- What else? Alimony.
- [chuckles]

01:50.750 --> 01:52.000
What'd they say, Dad?

01:53.708 --> 01:56.666
That I'm lucky to have
such a good helper like you.

01:58.875 --> 02:00.125
All right, you ready?

02:01.541 --> 02:02.625
[shutter clicks]

02:02.625 --> 02:03.708
- It's good.
- All right.

02:03.708 --> 02:06.166
Good. Here we go, bud. [grunts]

02:06.166 --> 02:07.750
Hey, honey. Honey.

02:07.750 --> 02:09.416
Get with Cooper. Let's get a picture.

02:09.416 --> 02:11.375
- Uh, you bet. Yeah.
- [chuckles] Oh, yeah.

02:11.375 --> 02:12.416
[Cooper] All right.

02:12.541 --> 02:14.916
Aw, Coop, Coop, Coop.
Do your thumbs-up.

02:14.916 --> 02:17.500
Yeah, you know,
given the state of everything,

02:17.500 --> 02:19.333
I'd prefer not to, if that's all right.

02:19.333 --> 02:20.666
Why not?

02:20.666 --> 02:21.750
It's what you're famous for.

02:21.750 --> 02:23.208
- Yeah.
- Drop it, Bob.

02:23.208 --> 02:25.875
We gotta... we got to get
this rodeo on the road.

02:25.875 --> 02:27.625
I can't thank you enough, Mr. Howard.

02:27.625 --> 02:29.458
Pleasure's all mine, ma'am.

02:29.458 --> 02:31.291
I hope your son had a lovely birthday.

02:31.291 --> 02:32.791
- Perfect.
- Yeah.

02:32.791 --> 02:34.041
Who's ready for cake?

02:34.041 --> 02:35.833
- [children] Me!
- [Cooper] All right. You ready, Janey?

02:35.833 --> 02:37.916
[children shouting]

02:37.916 --> 02:39.208
[Cooper] Come on. [clicks tongue]

02:39.208 --> 02:40.541
There you go.

02:40.541 --> 02:42.000
- Pinko.
- Yep.

02:42.000 --> 02:43.625
He still took my money.

02:43.625 --> 02:48.583
<i>♪ Happy birthday dear Roy ♪</i>

02:48.583 --> 02:53.416
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

02:53.416 --> 02:55.666
- [whistles]
- [cheering]

03:01.125 --> 03:03.666
<i>...that Los Angeles sunshine
coming through.</i>

03:03.666 --> 03:06.166
<i>Hal, I can't...
I'm sorry, I can't do this.</i>

03:06.166 --> 03:08.750
<i>I can't do the weather
if I don't even know if there's</i>

03:08.750 --> 03:10.750
<i>- gonna be a next week.</i>
- Only thinking happy thoughts today.

03:10.750 --> 03:12.333
[audio shifting]

03:12.333 --> 03:15.541
[announcer] <i>Sugar Bombs presents</i>
Grognak the Barbarian

03:15.541 --> 03:17.916
- and the Ruby Ruins.
- [children laugh, cheer]

03:17.916 --> 03:20.750
[TV show continues indistinctly]

03:23.208 --> 03:25.541
[groans] All right.

03:25.541 --> 03:27.541
[TV playing]

03:27.541 --> 03:29.291
[Cooper] I think that's everything.

03:29.291 --> 03:31.083
[sighs]

03:31.083 --> 03:32.791
Why wouldn't you do it?

03:32.791 --> 03:34.416
The thumbs-up.

03:35.625 --> 03:37.208
Oh, it's, uh...

03:37.208 --> 03:39.166
That's grown-up stuff.

03:44.291 --> 03:45.208
[smacks lips]

03:45.208 --> 03:46.875
Well, back when I was in the Marines,

03:46.875 --> 03:50.375
they taught us that
if they ever drop a really big bomb,

03:50.375 --> 03:53.041
told us to hold up your thumb
just like this.

03:53.041 --> 03:56.791
And if the cloud is smaller
than your thumb,

03:56.791 --> 03:58.625
well, you run for the hills.

03:58.625 --> 04:00.708
And if it's bigger than your thumb?

04:02.458 --> 04:04.291
They told us not to bother running.

04:05.333 --> 04:07.500
Do you think it's gonna happen?

04:08.958 --> 04:11.291
I certainly hope not.

04:11.291 --> 04:14.666
But us cowpokes,
we take it as it comes, right?

04:17.250 --> 04:19.000
[children laughing, chattering]

04:20.875 --> 04:22.541
Can I have a slice, Dad?

04:22.541 --> 04:25.125
You know what? Let me see

04:25.125 --> 04:26.916
if I can't rustle you up a piece.

04:28.333 --> 04:32.041
[TV playing indistinctly]

04:32.041 --> 04:34.375
[laughing]

04:34.375 --> 04:36.291
[door closes]

04:49.208 --> 04:51.041
[Cooper] All right,
one piece of cake coming up

04:51.041 --> 04:53.166
for my favorite cowgirl.

04:53.166 --> 04:55.750
Is it your thumb or mine?

05:01.750 --> 05:04.750
[eerie music playing]

05:10.208 --> 05:12.208
♪ ♪

05:19.750 --> 05:22.583
That's smoke, Janey. It's just a fire.

05:22.583 --> 05:24.666
♪ ♪

05:36.541 --> 05:38.541
[muffled TV playing]

05:38.541 --> 05:41.125
♪ ♪

05:55.416 --> 05:57.583
[rumbling]

05:57.583 --> 06:00.500
[intense music playing]

06:00.500 --> 06:02.583
[muffled shouting]

06:11.666 --> 06:12.916
[muffled] Let us in with you.

06:12.916 --> 06:14.583
[muffled] No room. Back off.

06:16.500 --> 06:18.500
[dramatic music playing]

06:43.083 --> 06:45.791
♪ ♪

07:13.958 --> 07:16.708
[♪ Perry Como:
"Don't Let the Stars Get in Your Eyes"]

07:16.708 --> 07:18.833
My name is Lucy MacLean,

07:18.833 --> 07:22.083
and I'm an active contributor
to the wellbeing of my community.

07:22.083 --> 07:23.791
<i>Repair Skills.</i>

07:23.791 --> 07:27.208
<i>I enjoy participating
in the Young Pipefitter's Association,</i>

07:27.208 --> 07:29.333
<i>which keeps me active.</i>

07:29.333 --> 07:30.750
Science Skills.

07:30.750 --> 07:33.375
Obviously, mine are nothing
compared to my dad's,

07:33.375 --> 07:35.958
<i>but I always relish a challenge.</i>

07:35.958 --> 07:37.916
<i>Speech Skills.</i>

07:37.916 --> 07:40.291
<i>My primary passion is
teaching American History,</i>

07:40.291 --> 07:41.500
<i>with a focus on ethics.</i>

07:41.500 --> 07:44.875
<i>I also participate in Gymnastics Club,</i>

07:44.875 --> 07:46.583
<i>Fencing Team C...</i>

07:48.166 --> 07:50.250
<i>...Intermediate Phys Ed...</i>

07:51.916 --> 07:53.250
<i>...and I dabble in Riflery.</i>

07:54.916 --> 07:56.250
<i>Though I'm not very good.</i>

07:56.250 --> 07:58.208
<i>♪ Change your mind...</i>

07:58.208 --> 07:59.541
<i>In my personal time,</i>

07:59.541 --> 08:01.000
<i>I enjoy taking walks</i>

08:01.000 --> 08:02.958
<i>and watching movies with my dad,</i>

08:02.958 --> 08:04.875
<i>gardening-- also with my dad--</i>

08:04.875 --> 08:07.541
<i>and participating in my family book club.</i>

08:08.375 --> 08:10.916
<i>We're still trying
to get my brother on board.</i>

08:10.916 --> 08:12.833
<i>He'll come around when he's ready.</i>

08:13.833 --> 08:15.791
My reproductive organs are intact,

08:15.791 --> 08:17.208
my hygiene well-maintained,

08:17.208 --> 08:20.208
and yet I have been unable to

08:20.208 --> 08:21.791
find a suitable marriage partner.

08:21.791 --> 08:24.333
At least, one I'm not related to.

08:24.333 --> 08:26.416
And we have rules about that for a reason.

08:26.416 --> 08:27.875
<i>♪ I'll ever love...</i>

08:27.875 --> 08:30.666
So, it is with sound mind and body

08:30.666 --> 08:33.416
that I hereby submit
my application to the council

08:33.416 --> 08:36.416
to participate in
the Triennial Trade with Vault 32.

08:36.541 --> 08:38.333
<i>♪ Don't let the moon break your heart ♪</i>

08:38.333 --> 08:40.416
♪ ♪

08:50.333 --> 08:51.666
[chimes]

08:52.708 --> 08:54.625
<i>♪ You're the only one ♪</i>

08:54.625 --> 08:59.000
<i>♪ You're the only one I'll ever love ♪</i>

08:59.000 --> 09:00.083
[sighs happily]

09:03.125 --> 09:05.125
[cheerful music playing]

09:16.333 --> 09:17.666
Norman.

09:17.666 --> 09:18.750
[beeps]

09:23.083 --> 09:24.666
[soft chuckle]

09:42.250 --> 09:44.041
♪ ♪

09:45.541 --> 09:46.708
Hmm.

09:46.708 --> 09:48.166
Feels a little tight.

09:48.166 --> 09:49.625
Won't be for long.

09:49.625 --> 09:53.000
On my wedding night, that dress got off
almost as fast as Burt did.

09:53.000 --> 09:54.125
Huh.

09:55.208 --> 09:56.833
[exhales]

09:56.833 --> 09:59.625
Oh, gosh. After ten years of cousin stuff,

09:59.625 --> 10:01.625
I'm definitely excited
for the real thing.

10:01.625 --> 10:03.666
Oh, Lucy.

10:03.666 --> 10:06.541
I am just excited for us
to raise our kids together.

10:07.583 --> 10:09.000
[soft chuckle]

10:21.041 --> 10:22.500
[chuckles]

10:22.500 --> 10:24.583
[optimistic music playing]

10:36.333 --> 10:37.708
[projector clicking]

10:41.666 --> 10:43.750
[pulsing, intriguing music playing]

10:54.500 --> 10:56.750
[chuckles] Dad.

10:58.833 --> 11:01.875
- My little Sugarbomb.
- Oh. [chuckles]

11:03.833 --> 11:05.416
Oh.

11:05.416 --> 11:08.708
Gosh, you look just like your mother.

11:09.833 --> 11:11.791
Yeah. I wish she was here.

11:11.791 --> 11:13.500
Me, too.

11:13.500 --> 11:16.500
Were you scared?

11:16.500 --> 11:19.166
- When you married Mom?
- Me? [scoffs]

11:19.166 --> 11:20.500
Terrified.

11:20.500 --> 11:22.166
[both laugh]

11:22.166 --> 11:25.375
Well, I'd never stepped foot
outside Vault 31.

11:25.375 --> 11:28.416
When did it go away?

11:28.416 --> 11:31.166
The moment I met your mother.

11:31.166 --> 11:33.500
[inaudible dialogue]

11:33.500 --> 11:35.208
[sentimental music playing]

11:38.458 --> 11:42.125
From that moment on, Vault 31
was a distant memory to me.

11:45.250 --> 11:48.333
Overseer, it's time.

11:49.750 --> 11:51.750
[optimistic music playing]

12:01.875 --> 12:04.000
[door whooshes open]

12:05.375 --> 12:06.958
[door stops]

12:11.708 --> 12:12.875
[Norm] Must be nerve-racking.

12:12.875 --> 12:14.875
Your husband could be anybody.

12:14.875 --> 12:16.125
I'm aware.

12:16.125 --> 12:17.500
- And as for his looks?
- Who knows?

12:17.500 --> 12:18.583
Big butt? No butt?

12:18.583 --> 12:20.125
But, of course,

12:20.125 --> 12:22.000
it's just superficial concerns.
It's what's on the inside that counts.

12:22.000 --> 12:23.208
That's right.

12:23.208 --> 12:25.041
And in that respect,
he could be a cannibal, or just like

12:25.041 --> 12:26.000
crammed full of tumors.

12:26.000 --> 12:27.208
- Norman.
- [door whooshes open]

12:27.208 --> 12:28.125
Sorry, Dad.

12:33.125 --> 12:36.250
[suspenseful music playing]

12:38.583 --> 12:41.208
[rumbling]

12:42.541 --> 12:43.500
[Hank] Gate-Keeper.

12:50.916 --> 12:53.000
- Chet.
- Honestly...

12:53.000 --> 12:54.833
textbook tumbler jam.

12:54.833 --> 12:57.833
It's gonna take some time to fix.

12:57.833 --> 13:00.333
Probably best
if we reschedule with the 32s

13:00.333 --> 13:01.541
- until maintenance and I can...
- Chet.

13:02.375 --> 13:05.250
What's going on?

13:05.250 --> 13:06.833
Lucy, I love you.

13:09.875 --> 13:11.500
We all know that, Chet.

13:11.500 --> 13:13.541
Messing around with your cousin,

13:13.541 --> 13:16.625
it's all well and good for kids,
but it's not a sustainable,

13:16.625 --> 13:18.791
long-term sexual practice, you know?

13:20.416 --> 13:21.833
Yeah, I know.

13:30.750 --> 13:32.041
[alarm buzzing]

14:01.333 --> 14:04.250
Welcome, neighbors from Vault 32.

14:04.250 --> 14:06.250
I am Hank MacLean,

14:06.250 --> 14:08.375
overseer of Vault 33.

14:08.375 --> 14:11.625
Lee Moldaver, overseer of 32.

14:13.125 --> 14:15.041
Thank you for your hospitality.

14:15.041 --> 14:18.083
Oh, we were sorry to hear
of Overseer Jackson's passing

14:18.083 --> 14:19.500
in your telegrams.

14:19.500 --> 14:22.250
When blight hit our wheat,

14:22.250 --> 14:24.500
we lost a lot of good people,
but this trade

14:24.500 --> 14:26.875
will help us get back on our feet.

14:26.875 --> 14:30.958
Yes, well, as arranged,
we offer you seed and parts

14:30.958 --> 14:34.125
- for machinery.
- In exchange, we offer you a breeder.

14:34.125 --> 14:37.125
So... [chuckles]

14:37.125 --> 14:39.333
who am I marrying? [chuckles]

14:39.333 --> 14:41.416
[tense music playing]

14:50.833 --> 14:51.833
I'm Lucy.

14:51.833 --> 14:54.500
Do you have a name?

14:54.500 --> 14:55.791
Monty.

15:01.458 --> 15:03.083
Lucky.

15:03.083 --> 15:05.000
[♪ Connie Conway: "Who Do You Suppose"]

15:05.000 --> 15:07.375
[applause]

15:10.958 --> 15:13.916
<i>♪ Who do you suppose ♪</i>

15:13.916 --> 15:18.041
<i>♪ I really love ♪</i>

15:19.208 --> 15:21.666
<i>♪ Who do you suppose ♪</i>

15:21.666 --> 15:25.625
<i>♪ I'm thinking of ♪</i>

15:27.583 --> 15:30.583
<i>♪ Who do you suppose ♪</i>

15:30.583 --> 15:32.708
<i>♪ I dream of...</i>

15:32.708 --> 15:34.166
So, what's your sperm count?

15:35.166 --> 15:37.041
<i>♪ And whose loving arms...</i>

15:38.166 --> 15:40.083
Uh...

15:40.083 --> 15:43.083
Your vault's doctor
must check every physical, no?

15:43.083 --> 15:45.625
I mean, sperm is pretty important
in perpetuating America.

15:45.625 --> 15:47.416
- [laughs]
- [Steph] Stop.

15:48.750 --> 15:50.250
[applause]

15:52.625 --> 15:56.583
Good evening and welcome
to the proud denizens

15:56.583 --> 15:58.041
of Vault 32.

15:58.041 --> 15:59.625
[applause]

16:05.291 --> 16:08.833
We are bonded

16:08.833 --> 16:11.166
not just as neighbors

16:11.166 --> 16:13.791
but by a shared duty.

16:13.791 --> 16:16.708
To keep the candle of civilization lit.

16:17.750 --> 16:19.666
While the rest of the world has been cast

16:19.666 --> 16:21.750
into darkness.

16:22.958 --> 16:24.416
Soon,

16:24.416 --> 16:27.250
if our measurements are correct,

16:27.250 --> 16:31.583
radiation levels on the surface
are dropping fast enough

16:31.583 --> 16:35.625
that the next generation,
Lucy and Monty's children,

16:35.625 --> 16:38.083
will be able to recolonize.

16:38.083 --> 16:40.208
- [laughs]
- [applause]

16:40.208 --> 16:42.666
- Whoo!
- [cheering]

16:42.666 --> 16:45.500
[Hank] Yes.

16:47.916 --> 16:49.666
After 200 years...

16:50.708 --> 16:53.708
...we don't know much
about what's up there.

16:53.708 --> 16:56.791
Desperation, violence,

16:56.791 --> 16:58.750
lawlessness.

16:58.750 --> 17:01.916
These survivors will need to be shown

17:01.916 --> 17:03.833
a better way.

17:03.833 --> 17:07.500
I'll admit I'm sometimes afraid

17:07.500 --> 17:11.583
that mean old world
will change us instead.

17:11.583 --> 17:14.166
But then I look at my daughter...

17:14.166 --> 17:15.750
[chuckles]

17:15.750 --> 17:18.708
[Hank] ...who's such a beautiful bride,
and her new husband.

17:18.708 --> 17:22.041
And I am not afraid.

17:22.041 --> 17:25.916
I feel hope.

17:27.250 --> 17:28.875
To Lucy MacLean.

17:28.875 --> 17:30.291
- And to this marriage.
- [applause]

17:30.291 --> 17:32.125
And to hope.

17:32.125 --> 17:34.625
[cheering]

17:34.625 --> 17:36.958
Let's dance. [laughs] Hit it.

17:36.958 --> 17:40.916
- [♪ The Castells:
"Some Enchanted Evening"]
- <i>♪ Who can explain it? ♪</i>

17:40.916 --> 17:44.791
<i>♪ Who can tell you why? ♪</i>

17:44.791 --> 17:49.791
<i>♪ Fools give you reasons ♪</i>

17:49.791 --> 17:53.416
<i>♪ Wise men never ♪</i>

17:53.416 --> 17:58.708
<i>♪ Try ♪</i>

17:58.708 --> 18:04.541
- <i>♪ Some enchanted evening ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Some enchanted evening ♪</i>

18:04.541 --> 18:09.541
<i>♪ When you find your true love ♪</i>

18:10.875 --> 18:14.833
<i>♪ When you feel her call you ♪</i>

18:14.833 --> 18:16.208
Let's dance.

18:16.208 --> 18:22.541
<i>♪ Whoa, across a crowded room ♪</i>

18:22.541 --> 18:25.291
<i>♪ Then fly ♪</i>

18:25.291 --> 18:27.458
<i>♪ To her side ♪</i>

18:27.458 --> 18:30.458
<i>♪ Then fly to her side ♪</i>

18:30.458 --> 18:32.208
[music fades]

18:35.333 --> 18:37.875
- [♪ Mari Jones with Johnny Moore's Band:
"Start It Slow"]
- <i>♪ So, listen ♪</i>

18:37.875 --> 18:41.333
<i>♪ My prince...</i>

18:41.333 --> 18:45.166
- [laughter]
- You're the worst.

18:45.166 --> 18:48.291
Show me to my new home?

18:48.291 --> 18:50.250
<i>♪ For you ♪</i>

18:50.250 --> 18:54.666
<i>♪ But love's got a right to lose ♪</i>

18:54.666 --> 18:56.583
<i>♪ So take my advice...</i>

18:56.583 --> 18:57.791
[Lucy] <i>This is us.</i>

18:59.833 --> 19:01.125
[door whooshes]

19:05.916 --> 19:08.583
Ah, isn't it great?

19:08.583 --> 19:10.625
Every big moment of our lives

19:10.625 --> 19:12.916
is gonna happen right here.

19:14.333 --> 19:17.416
Picture the Christmas mornings
around the tree.

19:17.416 --> 19:20.000
We have everything

19:20.000 --> 19:22.083
with the hand-me-downs;
an icebox, a blender.

19:22.083 --> 19:23.750
- They-they even gave us...
- [clothes hitting floor]

19:27.250 --> 19:28.375
Huh.

19:31.916 --> 19:33.250
Okey dokey.

19:33.250 --> 19:35.750
- [♪ Scatman Crothers:
"Keep That Coffee Hot"]
- <i>♪ Just keep that coffee hot ♪</i>

19:35.750 --> 19:36.833
<i>♪ Keep it hot ♪</i>

19:36.833 --> 19:38.166
<i>♪ Be sure to make a lot ♪</i>

19:38.166 --> 19:40.291
<i>♪ I'll make a lot ♪</i>

19:40.291 --> 19:42.250
<i>♪ Your coffee hits the spot ♪</i>

19:42.250 --> 19:43.958
<i>♪ It hits the spot ♪</i>

19:43.958 --> 19:45.875
<i>♪ So keep that coffee hot ♪</i>

19:45.875 --> 19:47.083
<i>♪ So keep it hot ♪</i>

19:47.083 --> 19:49.541
- <i>♪ I love your coffeepot ♪</i>
- <i>♪ I love your pot ♪</i>

19:49.541 --> 19:52.500
<i>♪ So keep that coffee hot ♪</i>

20:06.958 --> 20:09.041
[music continues in distance]

20:13.500 --> 20:18.083
- <i>♪ So keep that coffee hot ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Keep it hot ♪</i>

20:18.083 --> 20:20.833
- [fading] <i>♪ Be sure to make a lot ♪</i>
- <i>♪ I'll make a lot ♪</i>

20:24.791 --> 20:26.791
[ominous music playing]

20:44.208 --> 20:46.375
[♪ Carl Coccomo: "A Nervous Kiss"]

20:54.000 --> 20:56.666
- <i>♪ A nervous kiss ♪</i>
- [Monty exhales]

20:56.666 --> 20:58.791
<i>♪ That silent bliss ♪</i>

20:58.791 --> 21:02.000
<i>♪ The moon watched from above ♪</i>

21:02.000 --> 21:03.625
[chuckles]

21:05.250 --> 21:07.166
<i>♪ A million strings ♪</i>

21:07.166 --> 21:09.833
<i>♪ With notes that cling ♪</i>

21:09.833 --> 21:15.708
<i>♪ Play music to two hearts in love ♪</i>

21:15.708 --> 21:17.125
[wipes]

21:17.125 --> 21:19.125
<i>♪ Though I adored ♪</i>

21:19.125 --> 21:22.041
<i>♪ The times before ♪</i>

21:22.041 --> 21:25.666
<i>♪ They never felt like this ♪</i>

21:25.666 --> 21:27.750
[ominous music playing]

21:50.875 --> 21:52.916
Hello?

22:03.083 --> 22:05.958
[faint booming in distance]

22:06.958 --> 22:08.458
[grunts]

22:08.458 --> 22:10.958
[faucet running]

22:14.208 --> 22:15.833
[distant yelling]

22:15.833 --> 22:17.541
[suspenseful music playing]

22:33.666 --> 22:35.708
[woman screams in distance]

22:35.708 --> 22:37.250
[dramatic music playing]

22:37.250 --> 22:40.000
[peaking]

22:44.041 --> 22:46.375
[Lucy] You're from the surface.

22:52.791 --> 22:54.541
Raiders.

22:54.541 --> 22:55.875
[intense music playing]

22:55.875 --> 22:58.166
[grunting]

23:10.666 --> 23:11.791
[screams]

23:11.791 --> 23:13.750
- Ah...
- [high-pitched ringing]

23:13.750 --> 23:16.458
[muffled groaning]

23:24.833 --> 23:26.791
[Lucy panting]

23:26.791 --> 23:28.708
[Monty] Just so you know...

23:30.291 --> 23:32.500
...this was the best day of my life.

23:36.166 --> 23:37.250
[grunts]

23:39.375 --> 23:40.375
[screams]

23:53.958 --> 23:55.083
[knife slashes]

23:56.291 --> 23:57.541
[screams]

23:58.458 --> 23:59.875
[knife pierces flesh]

23:59.875 --> 24:01.250
[Lucy panting]

24:23.458 --> 24:25.958
[alarm blaring]

24:28.083 --> 24:29.458
[gurgles]

24:32.083 --> 24:34.916
[panting]

24:40.375 --> 24:42.500
[yells]

24:44.583 --> 24:47.333
[labored breathing]

24:47.333 --> 24:49.375
[dramatic music playing]

25:00.708 --> 25:02.041
[hissing]

25:02.041 --> 25:03.708
[grunts]

25:07.791 --> 25:10.791
[alarm continues blaring]

25:35.583 --> 25:36.791
[gasps]

25:49.125 --> 25:51.083
♪ ♪

26:04.000 --> 26:06.625
♪ ♪

26:16.750 --> 26:20.958
- [♪ The Castells:
"Some Enchanted Evening"]
- <i>♪ Who can explain it? ♪</i>

26:20.958 --> 26:24.541
<i>♪ Who can tell you why? ♪</i>

26:24.541 --> 26:29.250
<i>♪ Fools give you reasons ♪</i>

26:29.250 --> 26:32.333
<i>♪ Wise men never ♪</i>

26:32.333 --> 26:35.791
<i>♪ Try ♪</i>

26:37.458 --> 26:41.500
<i>♪ Some enchanted evening ♪</i>

26:41.500 --> 26:45.083
<i>♪ Some enchanted
evening ♪</i>

26:45.083 --> 26:49.041
- <i>♪ When you find your true love ♪</i>
- [yelling]

26:50.916 --> 26:54.625
<i>♪ When you feel her call you ♪</i>

26:54.625 --> 26:58.750
<i>♪ Whoa, across ♪</i>

26:58.750 --> 27:03.333
<i>♪ A crowded room ♪</i>

27:03.333 --> 27:05.958
<i>♪ Then fly to her side ♪</i>

27:05.958 --> 27:08.083
<i>♪ Then fly...</i>

27:08.083 --> 27:10.541
Get that jelly mold out of here!

27:10.541 --> 27:13.833
<i>♪ And make her your own ♪</i>

27:16.541 --> 27:18.875
<i>♪ Or all through your life ♪</i>

27:18.875 --> 27:24.166
<i>♪ You may dream ♪</i>

27:24.166 --> 27:27.083
<i>♪ All alone ♪</i>

27:29.625 --> 27:33.125
<i>♪ Some</i> e<i>nchanted evening ♪</i>

27:33.125 --> 27:36.375
<i>♪ Some enchanted
evening ♪</i>

27:36.375 --> 27:39.958
<i>♪ You may see a stranger ♪</i>

27:39.958 --> 27:41.541
[gasps]

27:42.791 --> 27:48.000
<i>♪ You may see a stranger ♪</i>

27:48.000 --> 27:49.916
<i>♪ Across ♪</i>

27:49.916 --> 27:54.166
<i>♪ A crowded room ♪</i>

27:55.166 --> 27:57.833
<i>♪ And somehow you know ♪</i>

27:57.833 --> 28:01.625
<i>♪ And somehow
you know ♪</i>

28:01.625 --> 28:03.291
<i>♪ You know ♪</i>

28:03.291 --> 28:07.000
- <i>♪ Even then ♪</i>
- [screaming]

28:07.000 --> 28:09.791
<i>♪ That somewhere ♪</i>

28:09.791 --> 28:13.041
<i>♪ You'll see her ♪</i>

28:13.041 --> 28:18.958
<i>♪ Again and again...</i>

28:18.958 --> 28:20.291
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Easy, pal.

28:20.291 --> 28:21.583
[grunts]

28:22.916 --> 28:25.333
Sir, please don't make me use force.

28:26.416 --> 28:27.500
[hissing]

28:27.500 --> 28:30.083
Oh, geez.

28:30.083 --> 28:31.291
[grunting]

28:35.583 --> 28:39.208
<i>♪ Some enchanted evening ♪</i>

28:39.208 --> 28:42.166
<i>♪ Some enchanted
evening ♪</i>

28:42.166 --> 28:47.125
<i>♪ When you find your true love ♪</i>

28:47.125 --> 28:49.708
[dark music playing]

28:56.833 --> 28:58.291
[yells]

29:24.833 --> 29:26.791
♪ ♪

29:55.125 --> 29:57.458
♪ ♪

30:25.666 --> 30:27.625
♪ ♪

30:40.000 --> 30:42.625
[steady beeping]

30:55.458 --> 30:57.416
[panting]

30:58.625 --> 31:00.375
[Moldaver] Welcome.

31:02.708 --> 31:04.666
[suspenseful music playing]

31:06.125 --> 31:07.375
Oh.

31:08.916 --> 31:10.833
I think I know who you are.

31:10.833 --> 31:13.833
Everyone knows who I am.

31:16.666 --> 31:18.875
But do they know who they are?

31:20.875 --> 31:22.708
They are the product

31:22.708 --> 31:26.541
of one of life's tricky little choices.

31:29.916 --> 31:31.583
So I'm gonna offer you a choice.

31:33.500 --> 31:35.041
Them or her.

31:35.041 --> 31:36.875
[somber music playing]

31:43.208 --> 31:45.500
[beeping]

31:59.875 --> 32:01.000
[Lucy] Hey.

32:01.000 --> 32:02.500
H-Hey, stop.

32:02.500 --> 32:04.166
- Dad. Wait.
- Lucy, please.

32:04.166 --> 32:05.916
We have to--

32:05.916 --> 32:07.958
- No. Stop.
- [door locks]

32:09.958 --> 32:12.166
You are my world.

32:25.583 --> 32:29.125
- Dad. Dad! Dad!
- [pounding on door]

32:30.125 --> 32:32.333
Stop! Stop it! Dad!

32:39.041 --> 32:40.916
You look like your mother.

32:46.083 --> 32:47.708
Where are you taking him?

32:48.708 --> 32:50.458
To the real world.

32:50.458 --> 32:52.416
You should see it sometime.

32:52.416 --> 32:54.416
[dramatic music playing]

32:55.500 --> 32:56.708
No, wait.

32:56.708 --> 32:58.291
Stop!

33:02.750 --> 33:05.291
Stop! Stop!

33:05.291 --> 33:07.208
Maybe you should do what you do best.

33:07.208 --> 33:09.875
- Stop!
- Run and hide.

33:10.958 --> 33:12.291
[beeps]

33:15.166 --> 33:17.625
[panting]

33:23.583 --> 33:25.583
[rapid beeping]

33:41.000 --> 33:43.083
[wind whooshing]

33:47.875 --> 33:50.291
[♪ Johnny Cash: "So Doggone Lonesome"]

33:51.000 --> 33:52.250
<i>♪ I do my best to hide...</i>

33:52.250 --> 33:54.541
- [all shouting]
- Hit him again.

33:54.541 --> 33:56.541
<i>♪ I try to make believe ♪</i>

33:56.541 --> 33:58.250
<i>♪ There's nothing wrong...</i>

33:58.250 --> 34:00.875
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

34:00.875 --> 34:03.333
Kickin' your ass. You like that, huh?

34:04.500 --> 34:06.250
[grunts]

34:06.250 --> 34:07.541
<i>♪ That you're gone ♪</i>

34:09.625 --> 34:11.625
Yo, let's go, let's go.

34:21.125 --> 34:23.416
[panting]

34:23.416 --> 34:25.041
[Dane] Hey. [grunts]

34:26.500 --> 34:28.250
How's your nose?

34:28.250 --> 34:29.875
[grunts]

34:29.875 --> 34:32.000
I can still smell, it's just...

34:32.000 --> 34:34.625
mostly blood.

34:36.333 --> 34:38.208
Flesh is weak, but steel endures.

34:38.208 --> 34:40.375
I-I know.

34:40.375 --> 34:42.583
[song resumes]

34:43.583 --> 34:45.375
- Come on.
- Yeah.

34:45.375 --> 34:47.833
Uh-huh. [grunts]

34:47.833 --> 34:49.250
Yeah.

34:52.708 --> 34:56.083
<i>♪ If they ask me, I guess I'd be denying ♪</i>

34:57.125 --> 34:59.875
<i>♪ That I've been unhappy all alone ♪</i>

35:01.125 --> 35:04.791
<i>♪ But if they heard my heart,
they'd hear it crying ♪</i>

35:05.833 --> 35:09.166
<i>♪ "Where's my darling,
when's she coming home?" ♪</i>

35:09.166 --> 35:11.291
[Felix] It is the duty
of the Brotherhood of Steel

35:11.291 --> 35:13.208
to secure the Wasteland.

35:13.208 --> 35:16.083
One day as squires, you will help knights

35:16.083 --> 35:20.083
find and identify prewar tech.

35:20.083 --> 35:23.000
Aspirant Maximus.

35:27.833 --> 35:30.875
Can you identify this relic?

35:32.625 --> 35:34.500
It's a... [clears throat]

35:34.500 --> 35:36.208
...rotor?

35:36.208 --> 35:37.708
[grunts]

35:37.708 --> 35:39.583
[Felix] A circuit.

35:39.583 --> 35:42.875
The ability to defend yourself
is but one part of your training.

35:42.875 --> 35:48.625
We are the finders and the preservers.

35:48.625 --> 35:51.375
Unless you know what to find and preserve,

35:51.375 --> 35:56.208
you are more useful as a corpse.

35:58.791 --> 36:00.625
[whirring]

36:03.541 --> 36:05.500
[atmospheric music playing]

36:07.041 --> 36:09.916
[quiet murmuring]

36:25.916 --> 36:27.875
♪ ♪

36:39.291 --> 36:40.750
Yeah, look at that shit.

36:40.750 --> 36:42.750
[dramatic music playing]

36:46.666 --> 36:49.708
- [aspirant] What kind of model is that?
- It's the T-60.

36:49.708 --> 36:52.041
Imagine getting to put on
one of those every day.

36:59.625 --> 37:01.916
Wonder why they're here.

37:03.916 --> 37:05.916
[officer] [over radio] <i>A-17.</i>

37:08.333 --> 37:10.291
<i>A-20.</i>

37:12.083 --> 37:13.708
<i>B-11.</i>

37:15.708 --> 37:18.125
<i>N-24.</i>

37:29.750 --> 37:31.000
[grunts]

37:31.000 --> 37:33.833
[insects buzzing]

37:35.291 --> 37:36.500
Come on, I got something
I want to show you.

37:36.500 --> 37:38.125
Latrine duty's a two-person job.

37:38.125 --> 37:40.625
[sighs] I said come on.

37:40.625 --> 37:42.750
That hole of shit isn't going anywhere.

37:48.208 --> 37:49.833
[laughs softly]

37:52.666 --> 37:54.958
[cans chiming]

37:54.958 --> 37:56.958
[atmospheric music]

38:24.250 --> 38:26.208
♪ ♪

38:42.041 --> 38:43.625
[Shortsight] Aspirant Dane?

38:45.625 --> 38:48.458
- Th-This was my idea. He didn't want--
- You're being summoned. Come with me.

38:51.541 --> 38:54.500
[somber music playing]

38:57.250 --> 38:59.208
[♪ Johnny Cash: "All Over Again"]

39:02.333 --> 39:06.541
<i>♪ Every time I look at you,
I fall in love ♪</i>

39:07.583 --> 39:10.166
<i>♪ All over again ♪</i>

39:11.250 --> 39:13.125
- [grunting]
- <i>♪ Every time I think of you ♪</i>

39:13.125 --> 39:15.291
<i>♪ It all begins ♪</i>

39:16.583 --> 39:19.166
<i>♪ All over again...</i>

39:19.166 --> 39:21.291
[whooping in distance]

39:21.291 --> 39:23.375
- [cheering]
- [applause]

39:40.458 --> 39:41.708
What's going on?

39:43.125 --> 39:45.416
A bunch of us were chosen to get anointed.

39:45.416 --> 39:46.958
[Thaddeus] Hey.

39:46.958 --> 39:49.250
- What's your title gonna be?
- Squire. To Knight Titus.

39:49.250 --> 39:51.250
And get this, we're going to the Wilds.

39:51.250 --> 39:52.791
- [cheering]
- Hell yeah, you are!

39:52.791 --> 39:53.875
[Maximus] Dane...

39:53.875 --> 39:55.250
[others] [chanting] Dane! Dane! Dane!

39:55.250 --> 40:00.458
Dane! Dane! Dane! Dane! Dane! Dane!

40:00.458 --> 40:02.500
[cheering]

40:02.500 --> 40:04.833
[laughter]

40:04.833 --> 40:07.625
[indistinct chatter]

40:12.083 --> 40:14.083
- [aspirant 1] Hey, you're next,
you're next.
- [aspirant 2] Yeah.

40:17.416 --> 40:21.000
[haunting music playing]

40:21.000 --> 40:23.500
[grunting]

40:25.583 --> 40:28.750
[shouting]

40:38.416 --> 40:40.666
[laughter in distance]

40:49.791 --> 40:52.375
[Dane screaming]

41:01.250 --> 41:02.791
What happened?

41:02.791 --> 41:04.791
[Dane panting]

41:07.041 --> 41:08.125
Give me that.

41:15.875 --> 41:17.833
[intense, ominous music playing]

41:28.750 --> 41:30.750
[♪ Connie Conway: "Brighter Side"]

41:37.041 --> 41:41.375
<i>♪ There's a brighter side ♪</i>

41:41.375 --> 41:46.041
<i>♪ To every dark, dark cloud ♪</i>

41:46.041 --> 41:50.958
<i>♪ And there's a smiling face ♪</i>

41:50.958 --> 41:53.208
<i>♪ In every crowd ♪</i>

41:53.208 --> 41:54.958
[groaning]

41:57.583 --> 42:04.500
<i>♪ All your troubles will soon fade away ♪</i>

42:04.500 --> 42:07.625
<i>♪ There's a brighter ♪</i>

42:07.625 --> 42:10.375
<i>♪ Brighter ♪</i>

42:10.375 --> 42:15.083
<i>♪ Side ♪</i>

42:15.083 --> 42:17.541
[indistinct chatter]

42:17.541 --> 42:19.000
[Reg] Everyone settle.

42:22.250 --> 42:25.208
I have a proposal for the assembly.

42:30.333 --> 42:33.041
We send a search party
to the surface to find my dad.

42:33.041 --> 42:34.291
- [grumbling]
- [man] To the surface?

42:34.291 --> 42:35.791
[Lucy] We can spare
four people from farm duty

42:35.791 --> 42:37.291
for up to two weeks,

42:37.291 --> 42:38.583
even with our dwindled numbers.

42:38.583 --> 42:41.000
Sorry, Lucy, but you're talking about

42:41.000 --> 42:43.166
opening the outer vault door?

42:43.166 --> 42:44.916
Just for under a minute.

42:44.916 --> 42:46.791
Okay? It's just enough time to--

42:46.791 --> 42:49.250
Okay, I-I know we're just...
we're brainstorming here,

42:49.250 --> 42:51.208
and there's no bad ideas
in a brainstorm...

42:51.208 --> 42:52.750
- [man] Maybe for you.
- ...but that's not something

42:52.750 --> 42:53.916
that we ever do

42:53.916 --> 42:55.875
or have ever done, never, ever, ever.

42:55.875 --> 42:57.041
I-I know, I know that.

42:57.041 --> 43:00.541
I know we're all hurting right now,

43:00.541 --> 43:02.166
but our first priority

43:02.166 --> 43:05.916
has to be to maintain
the security of this vault.

43:05.916 --> 43:08.791
That means not opening any of our doors.

43:08.791 --> 43:09.958
Well said, Betty.

43:09.958 --> 43:11.791
[Woody] Yes, thank you, Betty.

43:11.791 --> 43:13.083
Okay, let's move on.

43:13.083 --> 43:15.166
[Norm] They don't want to find Dad.

43:16.916 --> 43:19.375
If they did, they wouldn't
get to be in charge.

43:19.375 --> 43:22.333
[quiet, dramatic music playing]

43:43.541 --> 43:44.958
[sighs]

43:50.583 --> 43:51.875
♪ ♪

43:57.958 --> 43:59.958
[pulsing, dramatic music playing]

44:16.875 --> 44:18.208
Hey, Davey.

44:18.208 --> 44:19.500
- Hey.
- How's your day going?

44:20.500 --> 44:22.458
Bad as everyone else's.

44:26.875 --> 44:28.208
[groans]

44:28.208 --> 44:30.458
[mutters]

44:42.416 --> 44:43.666
[horn blares]

44:47.375 --> 44:49.375
[horn blares]

44:51.750 --> 44:53.458
[horn blares]

44:53.458 --> 44:55.541
[dramatic, ethereal music playing]

45:12.750 --> 45:13.916
[Lucy] Hold the elevator.

45:20.583 --> 45:22.916
♪ ♪

45:28.291 --> 45:29.291
Take care of Norm

45:29.291 --> 45:31.166
till I'm back, okay?

45:32.708 --> 45:34.625
I can't.

45:34.625 --> 45:36.875
I'm going with you.

45:36.875 --> 45:39.041
- Chet--
- What you're doing is insane.

45:39.041 --> 45:40.791
You don't even know which way to go.

45:40.791 --> 45:42.750
It isn't like the vault out there.

45:42.750 --> 45:43.791
It's big.

45:44.791 --> 45:46.500
[horn blares]

45:49.416 --> 45:50.833
Chet...

45:50.833 --> 45:52.750
I'm not letting anyone else

45:52.750 --> 45:54.291
get hurt on my behalf.

45:54.291 --> 45:55.916
Okay?

45:59.416 --> 46:01.208
♪ ♪

46:01.208 --> 46:02.875
Oh, Lucy.

46:04.833 --> 46:06.958
Oh, okay. There we go.

46:10.458 --> 46:11.958
[exclaims]

46:16.333 --> 46:18.875
I just tranq'd him.

46:18.875 --> 46:20.875
And I'll do the same to you
if you try to follow me.

46:22.291 --> 46:23.500
I'm too chicken.

46:23.500 --> 46:24.875
Thanks.

46:24.875 --> 46:26.875
[emotional music playing]

46:41.916 --> 46:43.583
[horn blares]

46:44.625 --> 46:46.583
[pulsing, dramatic music playing]

46:48.125 --> 46:50.083
[exhales]

46:56.166 --> 46:57.916
I'm bringing him home.

46:57.916 --> 46:59.458
[horn blares]

46:59.458 --> 47:01.750
[whirring]

47:01.750 --> 47:03.958
[horn blares]

47:05.750 --> 47:07.791
[horn blares]

47:23.416 --> 47:25.458
♪ ♪

47:33.875 --> 47:35.083
Stop!

47:35.083 --> 47:36.500
Lucy!

47:36.500 --> 47:38.875
Are you mad?

47:38.875 --> 47:41.666
Young lady, come back here right away!

47:43.291 --> 47:44.791
[Reg] Lucy!

47:46.916 --> 47:48.750
Lucy, no!

47:55.541 --> 47:57.375
- That didn't work.
- [horn blares]

48:01.041 --> 48:03.125
[tense percussive music playing]

48:14.083 --> 48:16.083
[door clanking]

48:19.291 --> 48:20.791
[gasps]

48:24.250 --> 48:25.916
[rad meter peaking]

48:28.833 --> 48:30.833
[ominous, eerie music playing]

49:00.916 --> 49:02.875
♪ ♪

49:15.708 --> 49:17.708
[waves crashing]

49:25.791 --> 49:27.791
[uplifting music playing]

49:46.583 --> 49:48.833
Okey dokey.

49:48.833 --> 49:50.500
[exhales]

50:02.875 --> 50:04.416
[gasps]

50:17.000 --> 50:19.041
[door closes]

50:19.041 --> 50:22.125
We have given you a name.

50:25.041 --> 50:26.333
Food.

50:26.333 --> 50:28.458
Education.

50:28.458 --> 50:30.500
A place in the world.

50:30.500 --> 50:32.500
So...

50:33.625 --> 50:35.958
...we expect you to give us

50:35.958 --> 50:38.541
the truth.

50:38.541 --> 50:40.708
Why did you join the Brotherhood?

50:41.916 --> 50:44.375
To hurt the people who hurt me.

50:44.375 --> 50:47.208
[mysterious music playing]

50:54.041 --> 50:57.291
I understand you're
a friend of Aspirant Dane.

50:57.291 --> 50:59.375
Yes.

50:59.375 --> 51:01.333
You're aware of their injury?

51:01.333 --> 51:02.583
Yes.

51:02.583 --> 51:05.083
Do you know who did it?

51:07.708 --> 51:09.708
No.

51:13.791 --> 51:16.458
Your fellow aspirants say it was you.

51:19.958 --> 51:22.458
No, I... [stammering]

51:22.458 --> 51:24.291
I-I wouldn't...

51:24.291 --> 51:26.083
Why not?

51:26.083 --> 51:28.166
Your friend was promoted, you were not.

51:28.166 --> 51:30.541
You have ambitions, don't you?

51:34.208 --> 51:36.208
[suspenseful music playing]

51:44.625 --> 51:45.750
[knight] Speak.

51:45.750 --> 51:47.750
[stammers] I didn't.

51:47.750 --> 51:50.083
I didn't do it. I did not. I...

51:58.833 --> 52:01.875
[stammers] I wanted it to happen.
Is that wrong?

52:07.083 --> 52:09.250
Yes.

52:09.250 --> 52:10.958
[chuckles]

52:10.958 --> 52:13.041
Yes.

52:13.041 --> 52:14.875
Violence...

52:14.875 --> 52:16.708
is merely a tool.

52:16.708 --> 52:20.666
We use it to bring order
to the Wasteland, but

52:20.666 --> 52:25.416
violence against a Brother of Steel

52:25.416 --> 52:27.791
is a sign of weakness.

52:31.250 --> 52:33.291
But are you?

52:35.500 --> 52:37.875
Weak?

52:41.375 --> 52:44.750
[stammers] I don't want to be. I...

53:02.916 --> 53:04.750
You have anything else to say

53:04.750 --> 53:07.208
in your defense?

53:19.041 --> 53:21.375
I just...

53:23.000 --> 53:25.166
I just...

53:25.166 --> 53:27.625
I-I want to thank you.

53:32.833 --> 53:35.000
[stammers]

53:35.000 --> 53:37.500
For your guidance and...

53:37.500 --> 53:39.416
for giving me a home.

53:39.416 --> 53:42.166
I-I had no place in the world.

53:42.166 --> 53:44.250
So...

53:47.666 --> 53:50.958
...if I can help
the Brotherhood make it better...

53:53.416 --> 53:56.125
...Eden or whatever...

53:58.541 --> 54:01.083
...even if it means giving my own life...

54:02.416 --> 54:04.416
...I'll do it.

54:10.333 --> 54:12.458
[heavy thudding]

54:12.458 --> 54:16.416
And I'd be grateful to the Brotherhood
for giving my life meaning.

54:20.166 --> 54:22.416
Good boy.

54:25.791 --> 54:28.666
Then you will be Knight Titus'

54:28.666 --> 54:30.666
new squire.

54:42.666 --> 54:44.666
[breathing shakily]

54:45.833 --> 54:47.833
[suspenseful music playing]

54:53.458 --> 54:55.458
[man coughing]

55:01.166 --> 55:03.291
It's not so bad.

55:03.291 --> 55:06.416
At least here no one steals your rations.

55:07.625 --> 55:09.666
They said I'll still have
a place at the Brotherhood.

55:11.166 --> 55:13.166
But I heard you got my spot.

55:19.083 --> 55:21.166
You know who did it?

55:21.166 --> 55:22.916
[sputters]

55:22.916 --> 55:25.041
Oh, I've narrowed it down
to any one of those assholes.

55:25.041 --> 55:25.958
[laughter]

55:25.958 --> 55:27.375
- [Thaddeus] Yeah.
- [aspirant] You like that?

55:27.375 --> 55:28.583
- No!
- There you are.

55:28.583 --> 55:30.958
- Ah! Yeah!
- Stop it!

55:30.958 --> 55:32.375
[aspirant] He likes it.

55:32.375 --> 55:34.500
They asked if it was you.

55:41.583 --> 55:43.625
Yeah, they asked me the same thing.

55:46.375 --> 55:48.750
I told 'em you wouldn't hurt a fly.

55:54.208 --> 55:56.541
[intriguing music playing]

56:02.500 --> 56:04.750
[Felix] Aspirant Maximus.

56:04.750 --> 56:08.625
It is your most sacred duty
to protect the Brotherhood.

56:09.666 --> 56:14.083
After which, it is your most sacred duty
to protect the mission.

56:14.083 --> 56:18.291
After which, it is your most sacred duty

56:18.291 --> 56:21.875
to protect your lord Knight Titus.

56:25.041 --> 56:27.958
Do you accept?

56:27.958 --> 56:30.291
♪ ♪

56:51.166 --> 56:55.833
Our mission comes from the highest clerics

56:55.833 --> 56:59.166
in the Commonwealth.

56:59.166 --> 57:01.375
It is believed

57:01.375 --> 57:03.125
that a denizen

57:03.125 --> 57:05.041
of the Enclave

57:05.041 --> 57:06.666
has escaped.

57:06.666 --> 57:08.833
[quietly] The Enclave's real?

57:08.833 --> 57:11.500
And that he has with him an object...

57:12.541 --> 57:15.583
...of profound potential...

57:16.916 --> 57:19.750
...to harm our nation

57:19.750 --> 57:21.583
or to save it.

57:22.583 --> 57:26.666
Each knight in this legion

57:26.666 --> 57:31.500
will search a section of the Wilds
for this target.

57:31.500 --> 57:33.250
Brothers...

57:33.250 --> 57:35.750
- [grunting]
- ...we exist

57:35.750 --> 57:38.166
for moments such as these.

57:38.166 --> 57:41.208
Go forth

57:41.208 --> 57:43.333
with honor!

57:44.583 --> 57:46.875
And may the shape of the future

57:46.875 --> 57:49.250
be cut by your sword!

57:49.250 --> 57:50.958
[cheering]

57:50.958 --> 57:53.791
Approximation of the target for your lord.

58:02.541 --> 58:05.375
You're dismissed, Aspirant.

58:08.375 --> 58:11.291
[dramatic music playing]

58:17.208 --> 58:20.041
[whirring]

58:36.458 --> 58:38.583
[indistinct radio transmission]

59:02.666 --> 59:04.750
♪ ♪

59:24.250 --> 59:26.000
- [gunfire in distance]
- [lively music playing]

59:26.000 --> 59:28.083
[cheering]

59:32.791 --> 59:33.791
[weapon launches]

59:33.791 --> 59:35.875
[groaning]

59:37.750 --> 59:38.916
[groans]

59:38.916 --> 59:40.458
[thud]

59:45.125 --> 59:46.583
[tense music playing]

59:46.583 --> 59:48.583
[Slim] How do we know which grave?

59:48.583 --> 59:50.916
[Honcho] Well, Slim,
we look for the fresh one.

59:55.791 --> 59:58.625
Dom Pedro has our friend
dug up once a year.

59:58.625 --> 01:00:03.083
Cuts some pieces off
and puts him right back in the ground.

01:00:10.625 --> 01:00:12.875
Bingo.

01:00:12.875 --> 01:00:14.041
Shit.

01:00:14.041 --> 01:00:17.416
You're telling me
this supreme badass we're looking for

01:00:17.416 --> 01:00:18.958
is a godforsaken mutant?

01:00:18.958 --> 01:00:21.625
Have some respec'.

01:00:21.625 --> 01:00:24.791
That's your prospective coworker
you's talking about

01:00:24.791 --> 01:00:27.250
and our ticket to a big payoff.

01:00:27.250 --> 01:00:28.750
Thought you said you knew this guy.

01:00:28.750 --> 01:00:30.708
I said I knew of him.

01:00:31.708 --> 01:00:33.583
My pop worked with him once.

01:00:33.583 --> 01:00:35.083
Your pop?

01:00:35.083 --> 01:00:37.083
How long's this asshole
been moldering in the ground?

01:00:37.083 --> 01:00:38.458
How do we know he's not feral?

01:00:38.458 --> 01:00:40.416
That is why

01:00:40.416 --> 01:00:42.083
- we brought...
- [clucking]

01:00:42.083 --> 01:00:43.791
...our little friend.

01:00:43.791 --> 01:00:47.166
A feral ghoul can't abide a chicken.

01:00:48.333 --> 01:00:51.166
If he goes for her, we kill him.

01:00:51.166 --> 01:00:53.541
[tense music playing]

01:00:53.541 --> 01:00:55.625
[clucking]

01:00:57.625 --> 01:00:59.625
[grunting]

01:01:02.041 --> 01:01:04.041
[groaning]

01:01:04.041 --> 01:01:06.000
- Whoa, whoa.
- [panting]

01:01:06.000 --> 01:01:08.041
[grunting]

01:01:12.166 --> 01:01:13.791
[jangling]

01:01:14.833 --> 01:01:16.958
[creaking]

01:01:30.708 --> 01:01:32.708
[coyote howls in distance]

01:01:34.291 --> 01:01:36.291
[eerie music playing]

01:01:37.916 --> 01:01:39.916
[breathing heavily]

01:01:41.916 --> 01:01:43.916
[leather creaking]

01:01:49.208 --> 01:01:50.541
[grunts, gasps]

01:01:50.541 --> 01:01:52.000
[shuddering]

01:01:52.000 --> 01:01:54.083
[coughing]

01:01:57.375 --> 01:01:58.750
[hawks, spits]

01:01:58.750 --> 01:02:01.666
[groaning]

01:02:04.708 --> 01:02:07.666
- [cracking]
- [groaning]

01:02:08.875 --> 01:02:10.875
<i>[vocalist yodeling]</i>

01:02:16.208 --> 01:02:18.208
[tense music playing]

01:02:26.958 --> 01:02:27.958
Ah.

01:02:33.500 --> 01:02:36.041
Well, well, well.

01:02:36.041 --> 01:02:39.583
Why, is this an Amish production
of <i>The Count of Monte Cristo</i> or...

01:02:39.583 --> 01:02:43.833
just the weirdest circle jerk
I've ever been invited to?

01:02:46.708 --> 01:02:48.708
[laughing]

01:02:52.583 --> 01:02:54.416
Welcome back.

01:02:54.416 --> 01:02:55.541
I'm Honcho.

01:02:55.541 --> 01:02:56.875
Now, you don't even know us--

01:02:56.875 --> 01:02:58.375
No.

01:02:58.375 --> 01:03:00.125
I do not.

01:03:00.125 --> 01:03:01.541
[clucking]

01:03:13.041 --> 01:03:14.916
Does that count?

01:03:14.916 --> 01:03:17.291
Sh-Should I shoot him?

01:03:17.291 --> 01:03:19.833
Would you shut the fuck up?

01:03:19.833 --> 01:03:21.166
We, uh...

01:03:21.166 --> 01:03:23.458
we got a proposition for you.

01:03:23.458 --> 01:03:25.291
A bounty came down.

01:03:25.291 --> 01:03:26.958
A huge one.

01:03:26.958 --> 01:03:28.541
Enough to be a...

01:03:28.541 --> 01:03:31.541
last score for me and whoever's with me.

01:03:33.000 --> 01:03:36.166
Yeah. Now, somebody made a run...

01:03:37.750 --> 01:03:39.291
...from the Enclave.

01:03:40.375 --> 01:03:43.208
Well, what makes you think
I'd give a good goddamn about that?

01:03:43.208 --> 01:03:47.208
It ain't where they's running from
I figured you'd be interested in.

01:03:47.208 --> 01:03:48.666
It's where they's running to.

01:03:49.833 --> 01:03:52.666
That witch Moldaver.

01:03:53.833 --> 01:03:55.666
In California.

01:03:56.916 --> 01:03:58.666
That's where you from, ain't it?

01:04:00.083 --> 01:04:01.875
Originally, I mean.

01:04:01.875 --> 01:04:03.916
<i>[vocalist yodeling]</i>

01:04:07.541 --> 01:04:10.375
Now, what the fuck would you know
about where I'm from?

01:04:13.166 --> 01:04:16.708
Well, that don't sound
like gratitude, do it, boys?

01:04:18.083 --> 01:04:20.166
How about we put you
right back in that hole

01:04:20.166 --> 01:04:24.166
so Dom Pedro can have his fun with you
for the next 30 years?

01:04:24.166 --> 01:04:26.708
[tense music playing]

01:04:26.708 --> 01:04:28.791
[breathing heavily]

01:04:33.125 --> 01:04:35.500
Well, I tell you what, boys,

01:04:35.500 --> 01:04:37.916
whenever somebody says...

01:04:39.000 --> 01:04:42.666
...they're doing one last job, that
usually means their heart's not in it.

01:04:42.666 --> 01:04:44.666
Probably never was.

01:04:46.916 --> 01:04:48.416
But for me,

01:04:48.416 --> 01:04:50.666
well...

01:04:50.666 --> 01:04:53.041
I do this shit for the love of the game.

01:04:53.041 --> 01:04:54.583
[dramatic music playing]

01:04:54.583 --> 01:04:56.708
[grunting]

01:04:59.125 --> 01:05:01.125
[whimpers]

01:05:01.125 --> 01:05:03.125
[gasping]

01:05:08.083 --> 01:05:10.458
[ominous music playing]

01:05:31.458 --> 01:05:33.333
[Ghoul] You right, friend,
about one thing.

01:05:36.291 --> 01:05:37.833
This right here

01:05:37.833 --> 01:05:40.750
was your last job.

01:05:40.750 --> 01:05:43.541
My paycheck wasn't quite
what you expected, but...

01:05:43.541 --> 01:05:45.916
well, you know what they say.

01:05:45.916 --> 01:05:47.916
Us cowpokes...

01:05:50.666 --> 01:05:52.375
[grunting]

01:05:53.708 --> 01:05:55.041
[thud]

01:05:55.041 --> 01:05:57.708
...we take it as it comes.

01:05:57.708 --> 01:05:59.958
[dramatic music playing]

01:06:09.458 --> 01:06:11.458
<i>[chicken clucking]</i>

01:06:13.375 --> 01:06:17.125
[♪ Sheldon Allman:
"Crawl Out through the Fallout"]

01:06:17.125 --> 01:06:20.333
<i>♪ Crawl out through the fallout, baby ♪</i>

01:06:20.333 --> 01:06:22.875
<i>♪ When they drop that bomb ♪</i>

01:06:23.916 --> 01:06:26.291
<i>♪ Crawl out through the fallout ♪</i>

01:06:26.291 --> 01:06:30.375
<i>♪ With the greatest of aplomb ♪</i>

01:06:30.375 --> 01:06:33.583
<i>♪ When your white count's getting higher ♪</i>

01:06:33.583 --> 01:06:36.000
<i>♪ Hurry, don't delay ♪</i>

01:06:36.000 --> 01:06:39.166
<i>♪ I'll hold you close and kiss those ♪</i>

01:06:39.166 --> 01:06:43.208
<i>♪ Radiation burns away ♪</i>

01:06:43.208 --> 01:06:46.333
<i>♪ Crawl out through the fallout, baby ♪</i>

01:06:46.333 --> 01:06:49.125
<i>♪ To my loving arms ♪</i>

01:06:49.125 --> 01:06:56.083
<i>♪ Through the rain of strontium-90 ♪</i>

01:06:56.083 --> 01:06:59.250
<i>♪ Think about your hero ♪</i>

01:06:59.250 --> 01:07:01.708
<i>♪ When you're at ground zero ♪</i>

01:07:01.708 --> 01:07:07.500
<i>♪ And crawl out through the fallout
back to me ♪</i>

01:07:09.875 --> 01:07:14.958
<i>♪ Why don't you crawl out
through the fallout back to me? ♪</i>

01:07:16.083 --> 01:07:22.416
<i>♪ Why don't you crawl out through
the fallout back to me? ♪</i>

01:07:22.416 --> 01:07:28.833
<i>♪ Why don't you crawl out through
the fallout back to... ♪</i>

01:07:28.833 --> 01:07:31.916
<i>♪ Me? ♪</i>

01:07:40.083 --> 01:07:42.125
[lighter flicks]

01:07:44.375 --> 01:07:47.041
Oh... hello there.

01:07:47.041 --> 01:07:49.500
Now, how about we turn on some lights?

01:07:51.083 --> 01:07:53.833
[jarring music playing]

01:07:57.125 --> 01:07:58.750
[Wilzig] <i>You need to go home.</i>

01:07:59.791 --> 01:08:02.125
Vault dwellers are
an endangered species here.

01:08:02.125 --> 01:08:04.791
I'm not going back without my dad.

01:08:07.166 --> 01:08:11.416
[Betty] <i>You could have destroyed
the last vestiges of civilization.</i>

01:08:13.083 --> 01:08:15.125
[Dervin] <i>What are you looking at?</i>

01:08:15.125 --> 01:08:16.750
[Norm] <i>A murderer in a cage?</i>

01:08:16.750 --> 01:08:19.458
[Dervin] <i>I don't know what
the people of Vault 32 were up to,</i>

01:08:19.458 --> 01:08:22.750
but it was anything but innocent.

01:08:25.708 --> 01:08:28.083
[Lucy] <i>What happened up here?</i>

01:08:29.083 --> 01:08:31.000
[Maximus] <i>I think everybody wants
to save the world.</i>

01:08:31.000 --> 01:08:33.083
<i>They just disagree on how.</i>

01:08:33.083 --> 01:08:35.458
[Lucy] <i>I wonder if anyone survived.</i>

01:08:37.041 --> 01:08:38.666
[Roger] <i>How long since you first started</i>

01:08:38.666 --> 01:08:39.625
wastelanding?

01:08:39.625 --> 01:08:41.833
A long time.

01:08:41.833 --> 01:08:42.750
[snarls]

01:08:46.125 --> 01:08:47.333
[Lucy] <i>What are you?</i>

01:08:49.291 --> 01:08:51.125
[Ghoul] <i>Oh, I'm you, sweetie.</i>

01:08:52.166 --> 01:08:54.666
<i>Just give it a little time.</i>

01:08:55.541 --> 01:08:56.500
Welcome.

01:08:56.500 --> 01:08:57.666
What the fudge?

01:08:57.666 --> 01:08:59.458
[Sebastian] <i>Forget Hollywood.</i>

01:08:59.458 --> 01:09:01.083
<i>You're a product, I'm a product.</i>

01:09:02.333 --> 01:09:03.625
<i>The end of the world</i>

01:09:03.625 --> 01:09:04.833
is a product.

01:09:04.833 --> 01:09:08.458
[Charles] <i>Vault-Tec is a trillion-dollar
company that owns half of everything.</i>

01:09:08.458 --> 01:09:10.708
[Cooper] <i>I guess everything's
a conspiracy, right?</i>

01:09:11.958 --> 01:09:13.875
[Charles] <i>Unless the people do
something about it.</i>

01:09:17.791 --> 01:09:20.166
[Ghoul] <i>Ain't much stays clean
up here, Vaultie.</i>

01:09:24.458 --> 01:09:25.791
<i>You'll see.</i>

01:09:26.708 --> 01:09:28.958
- [roars]
- [screams]

01:09:39.833 --> 01:09:42.208
[Ghoul] <i>You look out at this wasteland...</i>

01:09:43.208 --> 01:09:45.375
<i>...looks like chaos.</i>

01:09:47.583 --> 01:09:50.000
<i>But there's always somebody
behind the wheel.</i>

01:09:50.000 --> 01:09:52.083
♪ ♪

01:09:57.500 --> 01:09:59.708
[atmospheric music playing]

01:10:28.000 --> 01:10:30.458
♪ ♪

01:11:00.500 --> 01:11:02.958
♪ ♪
